     "caveat": "Large gains, losses and copy-neutral losses of heterozygosity (CN-LOH) carried by a share of the blood cells, from MoChA on the phased heterozygous sites of chr1 to chr22. In a UK Biobank study they became more common with age and went with a higher risk of a later blood cancer (Loh et al. 2018). That is a population-level association, not a diagnosis; an event is confirmed on a new blood sample. Below the floor nothing is reported, and an event above it can still be missed. Every MoChA call, with the reason it was or was not reported: mosaic/<sample>_mocha.tsv."
